Known bugs
----------

. the CGAL N ln N methods cannot handle coincident points. Events with
  more than one particle having identical rapidity,phi values should be 
  clustered with an alternative strategy. If this poses a severe
  issue to someone, it will be fixed.

. The Voronoi area evaluation (=Passive for the kt algorithm), is
  known to crash on events in which the momenta lie on a exact grid in
  rapidity,phi (i.e. a calorimeter). An unsatisfactory workaround is
  to slightly displace input momenta away from the exact grid.
  Work is in progress to address this issue.

. The CDF Midpoint algorithm runs extremely slowly when compiled with
  optimization. By default optimization is turned on for all
  algorithms, and the current build system has yet to be adapted to
  turn off optimization specifically for the midpoint algorithm. If
  this issue is relevant to you, recompile the
  plugins/CDFCones/CDFcode/MidPointAlgorithm.cc file manually without
  optimization.

